@nsobid-815A2C19D176789688FF33EA875C26C5

# Hyrule Warriors: Definitive Edition 1.0.1 - Double Buffering

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Forces a two-texture swapchain.
//
// KTGL's display setup fills a config block whose scan buffer count (3)
// becomes the nn::gfx SwapChainInfo buffer count, and the NVN window is
// built with that many textures. Using 2 instead lets the CPU run at most
// one frame ahead of scanout, cutting a frame of input latency. The
// renderer indexes its per-scan-buffer slots by the acquired texture index,
// so it never touches the third slot.

@enabled
002ABF64 49008052   // MOV W9,#2 for the scan buffer count (was MOV W9,#3)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Hyrule Warriors: Definitive Edition 1.0.1
// (Koei Tecmo KTGL, NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped; every site was
// located by structure and byte-verified against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
